  "assumptions": [
    "Current SC17/SC19 requires owned-unresolved422 step_not_resolved and direct-type-conflict409 type_conflict. Absent/foreign identities remain opaque404 unknown_step.",
    "The shared test fixture now uses valid fixed UUID identities for both definitions, preserving their short existing codes separately. Encoded sn1 input requires valid UUID components and the formatter takes a StepNodeRef object.",
    "Types are actual stored organization-owned fixture directory records; typed bindings are created through real HTTP with a persisted org-admin grant. The authored two-type conflict is explicitly a receiver fixture, not predecessor producer evidence.",
    "All existing explicit package values remain exact on safe unbind, including the sibling distinct allowance. Test configuration and snapshots are real SQLite/HTTP/Source; no fake router or admission owner is used."
  ],
